# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback: a direct load or refresh on a real,
# client-side route (e.g. /produit/<id>, /pro/seller/produits) has no
# matching static file at that exact path in most cases, so Cloudflare
# would 404 without this — instead it serves index.html (status 200, not
# a redirect) and the app's own router (src/store/AppContext.tsx) takes
# it from there using the real pathname already in the address bar.
#
# This never shadows the real static SEO pages generated by
# scripts/prerender-seo.mjs (dist/produit/<id>/index.html, etc.) or the
# sitemap/robots — Cloudflare Pages always serves an existing file at its
# exact path first, before falling through to this catch-all.
